Localized dictionary data
-------------------------
Jitendex Chinese community edition (greyindex/jitendex-yomitan-zh),
version v2026.08.11-zh.4, published 2026-09-27, upstream 2026-08-11.
Original Jitendex: copyright Stephen Kraus 2023-2026, CC BY-SA 4.0.
Community Chinese definitions are machine-translated and reviewed; they are
not native dictionary definitions or translations generated by this app.
Preserved notices: LICENSES/Jitendex-zh-NOTICE.md, Jitendex-attribution.txt.
Japanese and translated examples include Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR) material.
Embedded character glyphs: HanaMinA, see LICENSES/HanaMinA.txt.
Chinese content is converted to a restricted content tree, identical variants
are deduplicated with their applicable forms preserved, images use SHA-256
paths and static glyph SVGs are rasterized to PNG. No upstream CSS is executed.
Traditional Chinese explanations use OpenCC-js cn-to-tw conversion; Japanese
headwords, readings, quotations and form tables are not converted.
OpenCC-js licenses: LICENSES/OpenCC-js-LICENSE.txt and OpenCC-third-party.md.

Korean Wiktionary / Kaikki / Wiktextract: extracted 2026-10-15 from the
2026-10-01 kowiktionary dump. Text by Wiktionary contributors, CC BY-SA 4.0;
older text may also be available under GFDL. Original article links accompany
entries. Japanese-language raw records are preserved in the pinned compressed
source snapshot; generated data retains definitions and textual examples.
Ambiguous associations to JMdict are excluded rather than guessed.
Sources: https://kaikki.org/kowiktionary/ and https://ko.wiktionary.org/
Extraction software: https://github.com/tatuylonen/wiktextract (MIT; its code
license does not replace the dictionary data license).
See LICENSES/Wiktionary-data.md and LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt.

Generated and vendored dictionary data retain their original licenses,
independently of this application's AGPL license. Pinned source versions,
dates, URLs and hashes are recorded in dictionary.locales.lock.json.
